// lvim-zclaude — the lvim-zpm manifest. The board of Claude Code sessions: which exist, which one
// is running, and a jump to the pane it runs in. One keybind, tmux mode:
//   Ctrl s, then a  — open the board as a floating pane (or focus it, if it is already open)
// `{{wasm}}` becomes the absolute `file:` URL of the built wasm below.
//
// The four permissions, and why each is needed:
//   ReadApplicationState   — the pane manifest, the tabs, and `get_pane_pid`, which is how a
//                            running `claude` is matched to the pane it lives in.
//   ChangeApplicationState — focusing that pane, closing it (`X`), naming, sizing, hiding and
//                            showing the board's own floating pane.
//   RunCommands            — the one `sh -c` scan, the `kill` behind `S`, and the pane `N` opens.
//                            A plugin is WASI in a sandbox and cannot read `~/.claude` itself.
//   WriteToStdin           — `i`: the line typed on the board is written into the agent's pane,
//                            exactly as if it had been typed there.
//
// The key sends the board a MESSAGE (`MessagePlugin … name "open"`) rather than launching it
// (`LaunchOrFocusPlugin`), and `Esc` hides the board rather than closing it. A launched or
// re-floated pane always appears at zellij's default size first and is resized by the plugin a
// moment later — that is the flash. A hidden pane is shown by the plugin itself at its own size
// in one step, so nothing else is ever drawn. `src/main.rs` (`show`) has the zellij line numbers.
//
// **For the very first opening of a session to be flash-free too**, the board has to exist,
// hidden, before the key is pressed. That is what `load_plugins` in `~/.config/zellij/config.kdl`
// does (the same way lvim-winnav and lvim-zsession are preloaded there):
//   load_plugins {
//       "file:/mnt/development/biserstoilov/rust/lvim-zclaude/lvim-zclaude.wasm"
//   }
// Without it, the first `open` of a session launches the board (one flash), and every opening
// after that is silent. zpm does not manage `load_plugins`; it is read at session start only.
//
// Size and place, as shares of the screen (defaults 10%/15%/80%/70%): in the `payload` of the
// message —
//   bind "a" { MessagePlugin "{{wasm}}" { name "open"; payload "width=90%,height=80%"; }; … }
// or as the plugin's configuration in `load_plugins` (`x`, `y`, `width`, `height`). NOT as
// children of `LaunchOrFocusPlugin`: those reach the plugin as its configuration (checked in
// zellij-utils, `parse_plugin_user_configuration`) — they work, but only when the board is
// launched that way, which is the way that flashes.
plugin {
    wasm "lvim-zclaude.wasm"
    permissions "ReadApplicationState" "ChangeApplicationState" "RunCommands" "WriteToStdin"
    keybinds {
        tmux {
            // `summary_pipe "on"`: the fleet line is broadcast to the session's other plugins as
            // `lvim-zclaude-summary`, which is what lvim-zbar's `✳ 3 agents · 1 waiting` reads.
            // A configuration given here reaches the board only when it is launched from this
            // key; the durable place for it is the `load_plugins` entry in `config.kdl`.
            bind "a" { MessagePlugin "{{wasm}}" { name "open"; floating true; summary_pipe "on"; }; SwitchToMode "normal"; }
        }
    }
}
